d names, type reference depth and map-key rule, host closure, duplicate rule and 64-field limit. Explicit null for `wire`, `display`, and `summary` is admitted in both host tables, matching Rust. |\n\n## Complete row examination\n\nThe ledger identities and shapes exactly match the 686-row obligations for the three replacement/new profiles and the combined 2,416-row Rust/wire current inventory for final merge. The independent model-entrypoint crosswalk matches every ledger row by profile, model identity, current shape, and classification. No supported row lacks a case, exact input occurrence, or asserted result. All 22 unique referenced Rust cases resolve to actual functions in the current test source; all 64 upstream-gap rows have both control and refusal evidence.\n\n| Profile | Total | Exact `Supported` | Existing gaps | Aggregates | Explicit non-authority categories |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| browser-paired-replay | 686 | 665 | 16 | 5 | none |\n| coverage-selection | 686 | 665 | 16 | 5 | none |\n| coverage-execution | 686 | 0 | 16 | 5 | 594 `BLOCKED_CLI_TARGET_REQUIRED_OUTSIDE_SCOPE`; 71 `STRUCTURAL_CONFLICT_SOURCE_PROVEN` |\n| coverage-final-merge | 2,416 | 2,362 | 16 | 5 | 33 `BOUNDARY_CANDIDATE_SOURCE_PROVEN` |\n| **Total** | **4,474** | **3,692** | **64** | **20** | **698** |\n\nThe correction crosswalk independently reconciles to 3,692 exact entrypoint results, 64 existing gaps, 20 aggregate candidates, 33 graph-boundary candidates, 594 target limitations, 71 structural no-step tuples, zero unproved coordinate results, and zero implemented-awaiting-check rows.\n\nThe 33 final-merge graph candidates are source-backed: `coverage::generate` carries `EssIr` through `coverage_build::build` and synthesis, while `SemanticDependencyGraph` is separately minted and absent from `EssIr`. Their proposed `UnsupportedAtThisEntrypoint` disposition remains `authority_effect: NONE`; this review accepts the accuracy of the boundary evidence without adopting the policy disposition.\n\nThe execution ledger now makes no coordinate-support claim. For 594 representable suites, the actual CLI call reaches the closed `interpreted` target and receives its universal scenario refusal. The 71 remaining tuples have no `ScenarioStep` coordinate, as enumerated in `unresolved-policy-conflicts.json`. These two classes are distinct and exhaust the former 665 execution claims. They do not borrow Billing or library execution as coordinate evidence.\n\n## Seven first-review classes\n\n| First-review class | Final disposition |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Final merge generic attribution | Resolved. Final merge has 2,362 exact supported rows. The 1,697 reachable current-inventory rows are tied to concrete catalog edits and pinned complete changed, unchanged, omitted or refused results; the 665 replacement/new rows retain their coordinate-bearing family evidence. The separate 33 graph rows remain non-authority boundary candidates. |\n| 2. Selection carrier-only attribution | Resolved. All 665 supported rows select the generated coordinate-bearing suite through the real CLI route, retain exact parent bytes and requested IDs, and assert the complete changed or source-justified unchanged result. |\n| 3. Execution unrelated-scenario attribution | Resolved truthfully. Supported is zero. The 594 target-limit and 71 no-step rows record what reached the CLI and what could not be represented, without manufacturing execution support. |\n| 4. Browser unrelated replay attribution | Resolved. All 665 supported rows use exact projected values or complete source-justified unchanged models, with actual Firefox admission and one stepped authored scenario per variant. The periodic family additionally checks its complete projected contract and refusal grammar. |\n| 5. Stale S7 evidence references | Resolved. Every case-bearing field resolves mechanically to one of 22 current Rust functions; no stale reference remains. |\n| 6. Periodic content under replay/1 | Resolved. The producer emits replay/2 when any periodic binding is projected and retains replay/1 for event-only models. Periodic-under-replay/1, both causes, neither cause, unknown fields and all bounded vocabulary mutations are refused by Rust and Firefox. The retained pre-repair source independently shows an older replay/1 reader rejects replay/2 at the format field and periodic members at its closed binding grammar. |\n| 7. Nullable naming mismatch | Resolved. Six cases cover `wire`, `display`, and `summary` in both context and read host tables. Rust admits explicit null and canonicalizes it to omission; Firefox admits the same inputs. The production JavaScript uses nullable text admission rather than requiring text for a present null. |\n\nFor parent/child claims, the row mappings point to complete source groups rather than digest motion alone. The final-merge correction covers 186 component rows, 648 domain/type/entity/actor/view/conversion rows, 90 predicate/fact/quantifier rows, 289 command/outcome/event/error/effect rows, 76 binding/trigger/invocation/mapping rows, and 109 root/container/handle/reference rows. Their cases make one concrete authored change at a unique occurrence, pin complete output bytes or a coordinate-specific pre-output refusal, and distinguish semantic changes from full results unchanged after removing identity digests only. Parent rows rely on those complete finite child groups, not a generic Billing run.\n\n## Retained execution evidence\n\nThe retained receipts are consistent with the final source and are credited only for their actual boundary:\n\n- `36-full-ess-cli-package-final`, exit 0: the final S8 target passed 24/24. It records Mozilla Firefox 155.0.1, 21 Rust/Firefox periodic refusals, six nullable naming cases, and all source-family browser variants. The same package includes the separate 10-case coverage-browser and 30-case replay-fidelity-browser suites passing.\n- `33-current-catalog-combined-restored`, exit 0: 19 selected cu